    <section class="wrap" aria-label="Platform focus">
        <div class="metrics">
            <div class="metric"><strong>One control plane</strong><span>A coherent place to manage policy</span></div>
            <div class="metric"><strong>Policy first</strong><span>Intent before implementation detail</span></div>
            <div class="metric"><strong>Trusted edge</strong><span>Authenticated node communication</span></div>
            <div class="metric"><strong>Human-led AI</strong><span>Optional assistance, not authority</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="platform">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">The platform</div><h2>Network operations, brought into focus.</h2><p>Complex systems should not require a complicated experience. SAIFNEX is being built to turn network intent into understandable policies, consistent configuration, and actionable operational insight.</p></div>
            <div class="cards">
                <article class="feature-card"><div class="iconbox"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M4 5h16M4 12h16M4 19h16M8 2v6m8 1v6m-8 1v6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><h3>Policy &amp; protection</h3><p>Define the outcome you want. Organize rules, schedules, and policy profiles without exposing every low-level implementation detail.</p></article>
                <article class="feature-card"><div class="iconbox"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="13" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/><path d="M8 21h8m-4-4v4M7 9h4m-4 4h8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><h3>Devices &amp; networks</h3><p>Bring network membership, device enrollment, edge nodes, and their operational state into a consistent management model.</p></article>
                <article class="feature-card"><div class="iconbox"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M3 3v18h18M7 14l4-4 3 3 6-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div><h3>Intelligence &amp; visibility</h3><p>Build toward meaningful activity views, health signals, configuration history, and clearer explanations of what changed and why.</p></article>
                <article class="feature-card"><div class="iconbox"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 3 20 6v5c0 5-3.4 8-8 10-4.6-2-8-5-8-10V6l8-3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/><path d="m8 12 2.5 2.5L16 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div><h3>Trusted configuration</h3><p>Use an explicit lifecycle for generated, validated, staged, published, and deployed configuration—built to reject untrusted payloads.</p></article>
                <article class="feature-card"><div class="iconbox"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2m-9-9 2 2m8 0 2-2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><h3>Schedules &amp; automation</h3><p>Make recurring policy behavior understandable, reviewable, and consistent with the intent set by the network administrator.</p></article>
                <article class="feature-card"><div class="iconbox"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 3v3m0 12v3M3 12h3m12 0h3M5.6 5.6l2.1 2.1m8.6 8.6 2.1 2.1m0-12.8-2.1 2.1m-8.6 8.6-2.1 2.1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/></svg></div><h3>Optional AI assistance</h3><p>Help explain, summarize, and guide. AI remains optional, capability-approved, and outside the platform’s core security authority.</p></article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="architecture">
        <div class="wrap platform-grid">
            <div>
                <div class="kicker">How it works</div><h2>One clear experience. A carefully separated architecture.</h2>
                <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;line-height:1.85">The interface should stay approachable while the system underneath remains modular, verifiable, and ready to grow. The control plane coordinates intent; the data plane applies it at the edge.</p>
                <div class="principles">
                    <div class="principle"><span class="check">✓</span><div><b>Validate before publish</b><span>Configuration follows a defined lifecycle instead of being pushed blindly.</span></div></div>
                    <div class="principle"><span class="check">✓</span><div><b>Verify before activate</b><span>Nodes must check configuration integrity and trust before applying a new version.</span></div></div>
                    <div class="principle"><span class="check">✓</span><div><b>Keep recovery in the design</b><span>Failed updates should not silently replace the last known-good configuration.</span></div></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="platform-panel">
                <div class="layer"><span class="layer-no">01</span><div><b>SAIFNEX Control Center</b><small>Human-friendly policy and operations experience</small></div><span class="layer-tag">Interface</span></div>
                <div class="layer"><span class="layer-no">02</span><div><b>Control Plane · Laravel</b><small>Identity, networks, policy, lifecycle, orchestration</small></div><span class="layer-tag">Coordination</span></div>
                <div class="layer"><span class="layer-no">03</span><div><b>Signed Configuration Contract</b><small>Versioned snapshot, integrity hash, trust envelope</small></div><span class="layer-tag">Trust boundary</span></div>
                <div class="layer"><span class="layer-no">04</span><div><b>Data Plane · Go</b><small>Edge runtime, verification, policy enforcement</small></div><span class="layer-tag">Execution</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="capabilities">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">Designed for people</div><h2>Different responsibilities. One shared system.</h2><p>Access and controls should match the responsibility a person actually has—not force everyone to understand the entire platform.</p></div>
            <div class="roles">
                <article class="role"><small>Platform governance</small><h3>Developer</h3><p>Owns platform governance, system capabilities, integration boundaries, and the technical rules that keep SAIFNEX dependable.</p></article>
                <article class="role"><small>Network operations</small><h3>Admin</h3><p>Manages their network, configures policy, enrolls devices and nodes, and reviews status and changes.</p></article>
                <article class="role"><small>Everyday experience</small><h3>User</h3><p>Gets a straightforward experience with the protection and device controls made available to them.</p></article>
