    <section class="section" id="faq">
        <div class="wrap faq">
            <div><div class="kicker">Good to know</div><h2>Built with clear boundaries.</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;line-height:1.8">A few principles guide the product as the platform takes shape.</p></div>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details><summary>Is SAIFNEX only a DNS filter?</summary><p>No. DNS and policy enforcement can be part of the system, but the broader direction is a unified Network Intelligence &amp; Control Platform spanning network policy, devices, edge nodes, configuration, and operational visibility.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Does SAIFNEX require AI to work?</summary><p>No. AI is an optional assistant layer. Core security decisions and policy enforcement must not depend on an AI service being available.</p></details>
                <details><summary>How are configuration changes intended to work?</summary><p>Through explicit lifecycle states and trusted delivery: validate, stage, publish, deploy, verify, and acknowledge. A node should reject unsigned or mismatched configuration rather than activate it.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Is every feature shown here already live?</summary><p>No. This page describes the product direction and architecture. Some control-plane foundations and APIs are already in the repository, while the complete dashboard, Go data plane, production signing support, and operational integrations still require implementation and validation.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Are there subscription plans?</summary><p>SAIFNEX is not being designed around Free/Paid subscription tiers. Access may be subject to approval, while user-facing advanced capabilities are intended to be available without a subscription fee.</p></details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
